  "title": "Male fertility after age 35: What changes (and what doesn’t)?",
  "summary": "The myth that only women have a biological clock is misleading, but the research tells a more nuanced story. Male fertility after 35 does change, even if it doesn't come with the age cutoffs often associated with female reproductive aging. More American men are becoming fathers later than ever before:…",
